## Margin/Scale Analysis

The image print path used `margin_left_mm`, `margin_top_mm`, `scale_pct`, and `copies` from [silent_print_image()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/receipt.py#562-693). For the PDF path:

- **Dispatch challans**: All positioning is already baked into the PDF layout (`TOP_OFFSET = 57mm`, `ML = 10mm`, `MR = 8mm`) in [generate_dispatch_challan_pdf()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/receipt.py#299-560). No runtime margin adjustment needed.
- **Dispatch slips**: The PDF [generate_dispatch_slip()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/dispatch_slip.py#120-186) uses absolute coordinates within its 35×40mm page. The OS print driver handles page sizing. No runtime margin adjustment needed.

> [!NOTE]
> [generate_dispatch_challan_image()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/receipt.py#746-930) and [generate_dispatch_slip_images()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/dispatch_slip.py#188-279) are **not deleted** — they are only disconnected from the print flow. The only non-scratch callers were [open_receipt()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/receipt.py#932-947) and [open_dispatch_slip()](file:///c:/Users/Kevin%20Biju%20Kulangara/OneDrive/Desktop/laundry/utils/dispatch_slip.py#281-306), both of which are being updated.

